<title>LATVIA: STATE TO SELL MOST UNIBANKA SHARES TO FOREIGNERS.</title>
<headline>STATE TO SELL MOST UNIBANKA SHARES TO FOREIGNERS.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Latvian Privatisation Agency (LPA) said on Wednesday that it will sell 4.737 million of the 6.5 million state-owned shares of Unibanka to investors outside Latvia.</p>
<p>The agency said in a statement that it would make use of methods used on international markets to place the stocks.</p>
<p>The agency, which represents the state interests in Unibanka, owns 33.33 percent of the bank or 6.5 million shares.</p>
</text>
